# Sparse-checkout list for branch akio202607.
#
# Derived from the 41 shared libraries fcstrk11 actually builds, not from
# guesswork: every package below is one whose .so exists in
# .$STAR_HOST_SYS/lib there. Everything NOT listed is taken from $STAR DEV,
# which is correct because akio202607 does not change it.
#
# ~2830 of the repo's 18168 files, so about 16%.
#
# Copy this to .git/info/sparse-checkout (see instruction_akio202607.txt step 2).

# --- the forward upgrade itself -------------------------------------------
# StFcsClusterMaker StFcsDbMaker StFcsDiLeptonMaker StFcsFastSimulatorMaker
# StFcsPi0FinderForEcal StFcsPointMaker StFcsRawHitMaker StFcsTrackMatchMaker
# StFcsWaveformFitMaker
/StRoot/StFcs*
# StFstCalibrationMaker StFstClusterMaker StFstDbMaker StFstHitMaker
# StFstQAMaker StFstRawHitMaker StFstSimMaker StFstUtil
/StRoot/StFst*
# StFttChargeSharingMaker StFttClusterMaker StFttClusterPointMaker StFttDbMaker
# StFttHitCalibMaker StFttPointMaker StFttRawHitMaker StFttSimHitMaker
# StFttSimMaker
/StRoot/StFtt*
# StFwdTrackMaker (incl. the vendored genfit/KiTrack under include/Tracker),
# StFwdResidualMaker StFwdAlignmentMaker StFwdUtils
/StRoot/StFwd*

# --- packages akio202607 also modifies ------------------------------------
# StEvent StEventMaker StEventUtilities StEventCompendiumMaker
/StRoot/StEvent*
# StMuDSTMaker StMuAnalysisMaker  -- MISSING from the README's list, and the
# usual cause of "undefined symbol" at dlopen time
/StRoot/StMu*
# StPicoEvent StPicoDstMaker      -- also missing from the README's list
/StRoot/StPico*
/StRoot/StBFChain/
/StRoot/StDbUtilities/
# StChain -- NOT optional, and the failure does not name it. y2022c/ft2022c are
# registered through a StChain alias (PR28), so without this directory the
# geometry tag is unknown and `cons +StChain' cannot help: there is nothing on
# disk to build. Found by Diego and Barak, 2026-11-12.
/StRoot/StChain/

# --- geometry -------------------------------------------------------------
# StgmGeo1.xml carries the sTGC zplane int->float fix, FstmGeo the FST survey.
# StarGeoLinkDef.h lives here and the StarGeometry build needs it.
/StarVMC/Geometry/
# Holds only a README, but cons writes the AgML-generated TGeo sources into it,
# so the directory has to exist.
/StarVMC/StarGeometry/
# xgeometry -- the generator loads xgeometry.so explicitly (macro/sim/gen.C),
# and it is the third of the three build steps for a geometry change
# (StarVMC/Geometry, then StarGeometry, then xgeometry). Same report as
# StChain above.
/StarVMC/xgeometry/

# --- data, not code -------------------------------------------------------
# DB table definitions (idl) and the local survey/misalign tables. St_db_Maker
# searches ./StarDb BEFORE $STAR/StarDb, so without StarDb the job silently
# falls back to hardcoded geometry and looks like "the tables do nothing".
/StDb/
/StarDb/
# FTT data-window diagnostics (png/, root/). The per-run time anchors
# themselves now come from Calibrations_ftt.fttDataWindowsB -- 58 runs pushed
# 2026-10-16 -- so this directory is NOT needed to get the right windows.
# StFttDbMaker::loadDataWindows() still reads
# fttDataWindow/fttDataWindow.<run>.txt if it is present and then uses it
# INSTEAD of the DB, with a LOG_WARN saying so; that is for calibration work,
# and a stray file left here silently overrides the database.
/fttDataWindow/
# runab (the per-file job script) and the analysis macros.
/script/
# The single builder for the fGeom.root cache, for both Run22 and Run24, with
# misalign and FCS-material as arguments; it supersedes the former
# build_geom_run24.C, a near-copy differing in FCS material with nothing in
# either name to say so. Not the same as StRoot/.../macro/build_geom.C, which
# reproduces neither cache (sdt20211016, no misalign, no arguments).
/build_geom_misalign.C
/.gitignore

# --- deliberately NOT listed -------------------------------------------------
# No bare top-level pattern, so none of the personal scratch at the top of the
# repo is shipped: Xihe_response.txt, Xihe_suggestions.txt, the note_*.txt,
# forwardTrackingSummary*.txt, proposal_*.txt, summary_overall_alignment.txt,
# fwd_code_integration_plan.txt, instruction_akio202607.txt.
#
# That also excludes the 29 tracked top-level symlinks into script/ (runab,
# picoMatch.C, plotDilep.C, sim.C, ...). They are convenience aliases; use
# script/<name> directly, as step 7 does. One of them, plot_fcstrk_mom.C, is an
# ABSOLUTE symlink into /direct/star+u/akio/fcstrk11 and is broken for everyone
# but akio even in a full checkout -- a repo-hygiene item, not a sparse issue.
#
# Do NOT run `git sparse-checkout init': in git 2.26 it overwrites this file
# with "/*" and "!/*/", i.e. every top-level file and no directories, which is
# how the scratch files and dangling symlinks appear.
